<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.ReplaceAgentEnvironment(agent_id: uuid, transition: number, environment: string|uuid): number`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer llReplaceAgentEnvironment(key agent_id, float transition, string environment);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>The llReplaceAgentEnvironment function overrides the current region and parcel environment seen by an agent. The new environment persists until the agent crosses to a new region or this function is called with the NULL_KEY or empty string in the environment parameter for the particular agent, doing so will strip all environmental settings applied to this agent as part of the experience. This function must be executed as part of an experience.</p>
  <p>Returns an integer</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>uuid</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>key</span></td>
          <td>agent_id</td>
          <td>The key for an agent in the region. The agent must be in the region and must be participating in the experience.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>float</span></td>
          <td>transition</td>
          <td>The number of seconds over which to transition to the new settings.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>string|uuid</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>string</span></td>
          <td>environment</td>
          <td>The name of an environmental setting in the object&#39;s inventory or the asset ID for an environment.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

